From: written for wine-mac-builds
Source: none; a build fix for the tests.
Upstream: not yet (the same Makefile.in is unchanged up to 11.21)
Why: LLVM 23 (our llvm-mingw) turns floor() of a value it knows is not
 negative into trunc(). The dwrite tests import msvcrt, whose import library
 has no trunc or truncf (Windows' msvcrt.dll doesn't export them), so
 dwrite_test.exe failed to link: "undefined symbol: trunc". -fno-builtin stops
 the compiler treating floor() as something it can rewrite, as Wine already
 does for its own CRT (MSVCRTFLAGS). Only for layout.c, where floor() is used:
 EXTRADEFS also goes to wrc, which rejects the option.
Applies to: wine 10.0, 10.20, 11.x; changes only dwrite_test.exe (the -tests asset)

--- a/dlls/dwrite/tests/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/tests/Makefile.in
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 TESTDLL = dwrite.dll
 IMPORTS = dwrite gdi32 user32
+layout_EXTRADEFS = -fno-builtin
 
 SOURCES = \
 	analyzer.c \
